# examples/ui/06_style, played: the light theme switched on, a variant
# pressed and a disabled one that does not count, the page scrolled by the
# keyboard to its last control, and a theme of our own made and undone.
#
# The page is taller than its 800x450 window, so below the header it
# scrolls. It did not, until this script: its last two panels were below the
# bottom of the window, where nothing could reach them. See
# tests/e2e/script.h for the grammar.

# --- the happy path ----------------------------------------------------------

# A click on Light Theme: one line in the example, and every control on the
# page changes with it. The colours fade over 0.12 s; a shot waits for them.
3 click 368 57
16 shot light_theme

# Start game counts a press...
17 click 126 216

# --- the failure path: a disabled button --------------------------------------

# ...and Continue, disabled, does not.
19 click 223 272
30 shot pressed_once

# --- the page, by the keyboard -------------------------------------------------

# Up from the first control comes round to the last, Excitement, at the
# bottom of the page: the page scrolls to show it. Two steps right, 35% to
# 45%, and the bar above it follows.
31 tap KEY_UP
33 tap KEY_RIGHT
35 tap KEY_RIGHT
46 shot excitement_in_view

# Your own theme: a gold accent, copied from the current theme and set back;
# Reset builds the light one again.
47 click 130 297
60 shot gold_accent
61 click 698 297
74 shot reset
74 end
